Subject: Check `CapacityBuffer` readiness during reactive scale-up and capacity-constraint triage

Why: `CapacityBuffer` placeholder pods under `buffer.x-k8s.io/active-capacity` live only inside Cluster Autoscaler memory (`kubectl get pods` shows 0 Pending pods), so upstream's skill gave no command or condition table for diagnosing unprovisioned or failing buffers and described placeholders as real evicted pods. Adding `CapacityBuffer` triage discovery to the frontmatter description, aligning the placeholder description across `SKILL.md` and `assets/capacity-buffer-serving.yaml`, and documenting `kubectl get capacitybuffers.autoscaling.x-k8s.io -A`, the `v1beta1` condition triad (`ReadyForProvisioning=False`, `LimitedByQuotas=True`, `Provisioning=False`, plus steady-state `Provisioning=True` / `FakePodsInjected`), and `NotTriggerScaleUp` events on the `CapacityBuffer` object lets reactive triage report failing standby buffers on the target `ComputeClass`.
Local-Issue: #2635
Eval-Case: autoscaler-capacity-buffer-triage-probe
Retire-When: upstream's `gke-cluster-autoscaler` skill documents `kubectl get capacitybuffers.autoscaling.x-k8s.io -A`, the in-memory placeholder model, and the `v1beta1` `ReadyForProvisioning`, `LimitedByQuotas`, and `Provisioning` triage conditions with `NotTriggerScaleUp` event inspection

